      "labels": [
        "Section"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "section_id": "section-2",
        "title": "Introduccion",
        "level": 2,
        "order": 2,
        "heading_type": "numbered",
        "numbering": "1",
        "start_line": 3,
        "end_line": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "chunk:cf930a8d0f9b30a7:chunk-1",
      "labels": [
        "Chunk"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "chunk_id": "chunk-1",
        "text": "La biologia celular estudia la estructura y funcion de las celulas. La celula es la unidad basica de los seres vivos y contiene componentes especializados.",
        "order": 1,
        "start_line": 5,
        "end_line": 5,
        "word_count": 25,
        "character_count": 155,
        "chunk_type": "paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "section:cf930a8d0f9b30a7:section-3",
      "labels": [
        "Section"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "section_id": "section-3",
        "title": "Membrana celular",
        "level": 3,
        "order": 3,
        "heading_type": "numbered",
        "numbering": "1.1",
        "start_line": 7,
        "end_line": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "chunk:cf930a8d0f9b30a7:chunk-2",
      "labels": [
        "Chunk"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "chunk_id": "chunk-2",
        "text": "La membrana celular regula el intercambio de sustancias. Esta formada por una bicapa lipidica y proteinas que participan en transporte, senalizacion y reconocimiento.",
        "order": 2,
        "start_line": 9,
        "end_line": 9,
        "word_count": 23,
        "character_count": 166,
        "chunk_type": "paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "section:cf930a8d0f9b30a7:section-4",
      "labels": [
        "Section"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "section_id": "section-4",
        "title": "Organelos",
        "level": 3,
        "order": 4,
        "heading_type": "numbered",
        "numbering": "1.2",
        "start_line": 11,
        "end_line": 13
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "chunk:cf930a8d0f9b30a7:chunk-3",
      "labels": [
        "Chunk"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "chunk_id": "chunk-3",
        "text": "Los organelos realizan tareas especificas. El nucleo guarda informacion genetica, las mitocondrias producen energia y los ribosomas participan en la sintesis de proteinas.",
        "order": 3,
        "start_line": 13,
        "end_line": 13,
        "word_count": 23,
        "character_count": 171,
        "chunk_type": "paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "section:cf930a8d0f9b30a7:section-5",
      "labels": [
        "Section"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "section_id": "section-5",
        "title": "Resumen de temas importantes",
        "level": 2,
        "order": 5,
        "heading_type": "numbered",
        "numbering": "2",
        "start_line": 15,
        "end_line": 17
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "chunk:cf930a8d0f9b30a7:chunk-4",
      "labels": [
        "Chunk"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "chunk_id": "chunk-4",
        "text": "Los conceptos clave son celula, membrana celular, organelos, nucleo, mitocondria y sintesis de proteinas.",
        "order": 4,
        "start_line": 17,
        "end_line": 17,
        "word_count": 14,
        "character_count": 105,
        "chunk_type": "paragraph"
      }
    },
